WEBVTT

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:11.800
"Second High School
Cultural Festival"

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.340
Yo.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:15.050
"No rampages"

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:15.050
Hirano-senpai.

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:21.140
"Hooligan Fortune Café"

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:21.140
The café is hooligan themed, so our
language ain't nice, but we're chill.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:22.980
"Hooligan Fortune Café"

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:22.980
You always talk this way, though.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:24.230
Shut it, Sasaki!

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:27.400
Stop slacking and go take orders.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.270
So, what do you want?

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:31.530
I'd like coffee, please.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.190
No food?

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:35.280
I'm going to eat after this.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.990
Huh. Sit tight.

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:43.460
Their class sure is interesting.
Hooligans are taking orders.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.830
"Fortune Tent"

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.830
Is the fortune teller a hooligan, too?

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:49.130
Miyano. Here.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:50.000
Thank you so m--

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.590
"Customers. Bring 'em on."

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:53.470
"Customers. Bring 'em on."
Scary.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:54.510
All done.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:57.720
Welcome back. What did you ask about?

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:02.470
The gorgeous pop idol or the
gorgeous manager's perspective.

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:05.810
I wasn't sure which
of the two manga to buy.

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:09.020
I was told to pick
the one I felt closer to,

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.780
so I settled on the pop idol,
who's closer in age.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.360
Kuresawa, are you a <i>fudanshi</i>?

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.660
No. I'm a boyfriend who does his homework.

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:39.510
"Sasaki and Miyano"

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:49.540
"Fortune Hut"

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:51.540
"Fortune Hut"
"Episode 10: 'Love.'"

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:51.540
Hey there. Good to see you.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:58.510
It looks good. You're not
dressed as a hooligan.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:03.430
I intended to, but everyone
told me it was too scary.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:05.890
How did he accomplish that?

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:08.890
How could they say that
about this sweet face?

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:12.270
The mask is making it even more ominous.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:17.900
Now then, I use the tarot to find
a solution to a problem you have.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.400
The crystal ball is irrelevant...

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.950
And the cards are a special set
designed by the class!

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:27.540
They went all out.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:30.460
Do you have a problem you need to solve?

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:34.500
Like how to land a date with your crush?

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:39.420
Or where you should take your
crush to confess your feelings?

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:41.970
The more concrete the better.

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:44.260
Why are they all romance related?

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.600
Hormones, I guess.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:53.980
Come on. Pretend I'm some
random fortune teller and confess.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:55.520
You'll feel better.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:57.360
An interrogation?

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.610
Well, for example,

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:05.990
when you aren't confident how you feel,
how do you gain that confidence?

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:08.740
Confidence, huh?

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:10.620
Start by mixing the cards.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:11.540
Okay.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:17.090
Now mix them the other way while thinking,
"I want to have confidence."

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:20.630
And choose a card to flip over.

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:21.760
Okay.

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:26.510
"Strength"

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:26.510
This card signifies...

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:28.640
...persistence.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:30.680
Persistence?

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:35.190
Perhaps you have been trying various
things so you can have confidence?

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:39.610
Does that resonate with you?

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:45.450
I don't want to proceed
despite my lack of confidence

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:49.240
and then find out that I was wrong.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:53.080
You're so earnest.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:57.630
You would be a good fit as the next
Discipline Committee Chairman.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.250
No thanks.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:01.170
That was fast.

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:05.260
Usually you can state your
feelings clearly like that.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:08.930
That you're struggling with this...

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:14.310
Perhaps it's a concern that arose over
a worldview you've never held before.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:20.900
It shows just how important
this issue is to you.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:27.660
I think it's perfectly natural
to lack confidence.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:32.330
You can see the finish line
ahead of you, right?

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:34.450
Don't give up.

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:38.250
Keep pushing forward!

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:39.630
I will!

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:43.050
Well, that's all for this reading.

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:44.920
Thank you, Chairman.

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:50.140
"Bring it"
"Strength"

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:54.100
"Bring it"
"Strength"

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:54.100
For romance, it would signify...

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:57.440
...a love that slowly ripens over time.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:59.100
Ooh, that was good!

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:04.360
I hope it goes well for Miyano.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:06.440
Up to the other person, though.

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:10.070
Now then, what should <i>I </i>do?

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:13.660
Accept it without resistance.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:17.210
"The Hanged Man"

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:17.210
Accept it without resistance.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:23.670
My dear big brother.

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:25.300
That was delicious.

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:27.010
Thanks for coming.

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:29.180
You have plans now, right?

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:30.300
Yeah.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.550
See you at the competition then.

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:35.060
Sasaki, your shift is over, isn't it?

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:36.770
It is?

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:38.600
Go get changed.

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:39.640
Okay.

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:43.730
Mya-chan, wait a moment
while I get changed.

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:44.820
Oh, okay.

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:46.530
He had ten more minutes, though.

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:48.450
It's just ten minutes.

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:51.410
And get back in your tent.

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:59.620
Huh? Wow, Hirano!

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:02.000
You look like a hooligan! It suits you!

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:06.710
Hey, Kagi-kun. Drop some cash here.
I'll treat you to a drink.

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:07.590
Okay!

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:11.090
"Pork Skewers"

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:15.850
--Mya-chan, class 1-B--
--Senpai, class 1-C--

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:19.770
You first.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:23.270
Class 1-C is doing
a cotton candy experience.

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:27.230
1-B is doing Guess the Spiciest Treat.

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:29.900
Wanna do both after the competition?

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:31.110
Yes!

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:32.990
You have to get changed now?

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:33.870
Yes.

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:35.990
Okay. Good luck.

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:36.580
Thanks.

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:37.870
"You're the star!!"
"Miss Actress Competition"

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:37.870
Thanks.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:39.330
"You're the star!!"
"Miss Actress Competition"

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:39.330
The next contestant is the princess
of class 1-D, Ms. Sato!

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:43.120
The next contestant is the princess
of class 1-D, Ms. Sato!

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:47.500
--I didn't like the idea, but I think
I managed to be supportive.
--My, you look lovely.
Do you have a concept?

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:48.670
--I'm glad.
--My, you look lovely.
Do you have a concept?

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:51.130
Hello, Sasaki-senpai.

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:52.760
Hey.

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:54.590
You're watching from here?

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:57.850
Yeah. You're not competing, right?

00:07:57.850 --> 00:07:59.140
Correct.

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:01.390
Oh, Miyano's next.

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:18.700
He's wearing makeup?

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:21.250
Hanzawa-senpai did it for him.

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:22.710
Oh...

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:30.380
Can you support Miyano appearing
in a cross-dressing competition like this?

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:32.800
How much do you know?

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:35.720
He hasn't told me anything.

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:37.720
I got a distinct impression, though.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:40.390
Well, that makes sense.

00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:42.770
I never did hide it.

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:47.440
I mean, I don't exactly
feel great about it.

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:50.480
But I like seeing Mya-chan enjoy himself.

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:55.450
That's how it started.

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:59.450
From 2-B we have, um, Miss Yumi Miyano?

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:02.700
Yumi-chan!

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:04.160
It's Yoshikazu.

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:06.420
I completely misread that. My apologies.

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:10.460
--You boys there already knew.
--I like when he looks happy.

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:14.590
I ap-appreciate the support of 2-B!

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:16.550
He tripped up on his line.

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:19.050
You all thought up lines for him?

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:24.890
Yes. We were fired up about winning,
so lines were debated during lunch.

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:29.730
Mya-chan is so kind.

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:33.110
Even after learning
my feelings, he's still kind.

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:38.780
And when I'm 50, I might look
totally different than I do now

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:40.330
Wait...

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:41.950
Does that mean...

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:47.870
...he's considering me that long-term?

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:51.590
Are you all right?

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:53.590
Y-Yeah.

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:59.340
A... figure of speech or something?
Probably nothing more.

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:02.010
I like him.

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:04.890
I wanna grow up.

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:10.190
So I don't bring us both down, I wanna be

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:12.320
a cool adult.

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:17.650
"Miss Fujisawa"

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:17.650
This concludes the Miss Actress
Competition. Until next year!

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:18.530
"Runner-up"

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:18.530
This concludes the Miss Actress
Competition. Until next year!

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:20.990
"Runner-up"

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:20.990
I lost. Sorry.

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:24.540
Well, I hate to admit it,
but first place was incredible.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:27.000
Maybe we should be more direct.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:29.500
Then next year, we'll
captivate them with Tasuko.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:33.630
Don't say that! Tasuko is banned!

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:34.750
Senpai.

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:36.880
Good work, Mya-chan.

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:38.300
Too bad you lost.

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:44.180
I'm kinda disappointed, but also kinda
glad I looked manlier than first place.

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:46.220
You did get taller.

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:48.520
That's right! I'm taller now.

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:50.020
A year ago you were here.

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:53.310
I wasn't <i>that </i>short.

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:57.400
And you changed your hair.

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:57.320
It looks nice.

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:02.450
Um...

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:08.330
Miyano, time to get changed.

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:10.370
Oh, uh, see you soon.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:12.420
Yeah. See ya soon.

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:24.010
He was... self-conscious.

00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:29.060
--The festival will come to a close
soon. Enjoy it to the end!

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:31.640
--A lot of people stayed.
--The festival will come to a close
soon. Enjoy it to the end!

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:35.610
--Senpai, you don't need
to participate in the closing?
--The festival will come to a close
soon. Enjoy it to the end!

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:40.200
Nah. There's nothing to do
for my class. Besides...

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:43.410
I wanna be with you, Mya-chan.

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:44.780
Uh...

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:48.910
Um, I...

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:57.550
That startled me.

00:11:57.550 --> 00:12:00.920
Are these closing fireworks?
First time I've seen 'em.

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:02.430
In your three years?

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:06.600
Yup. I would always leave
before the closing.

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:12.020
But this year, I had you with me,
so it was the festival of them all.

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:20.610
Could you... wait just a little
longer for my answer?

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:24.450
It feels irresponsible
to give it right now.

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:27.660
So then...

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:33.290
...how much...

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:36.210
Sure.

00:12:36.210 --> 00:12:39.130
My heart is so loud.

00:12:39.130 --> 00:12:43.090
How much can I touch him?

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:48.350
I just... don't know anymore.

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:53.770
I'll be waiting.

00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:05.660
I'll be waiting.

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:09.280
He's being vulnerable.

00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:16.120
I like it when he does that.

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:19.840
I wanted to hug him then.

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:23.880
I wanted to take care of him.

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:30.140
Do I like him the same way he likes me?

00:13:30.140 --> 00:13:33.310
I'm happy I'm needed.

00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:41.940
I'm happy he enjoys my hobby with me.

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:44.440
That's not all it is.

00:13:45.860 --> 00:13:48.570
I can't say it yet.

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:51.330
I don't want to hurt him.

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:54.450
I can't just try it and find out.

00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:57.420
I don't want to decide I was mistaken.

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:03.800
Is it just the first floor
left to lock up?

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:06.220
Uh, yes.

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:08.720
It would be irresponsible to say it

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:11.850
without knowing for certain
I won't hurt him.

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:15.310
Shall we go? Hirano could get mad.

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:20.610
He appreciates me. So much.

00:14:22.230 --> 00:14:24.480
This room is messy.

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:26.650
It was the prep room
for the stage performance.

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:30.570
Oh. Yeah, lots of people were in that.

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:31.830
I want to say it.

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:33.830
What will the next room be like?

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:36.120
--Hopefully it's tidy for the inspection.

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:41.080
--I don't know if this is the same
way Senpai feels about me.
--Hopefully it's tidy for the inspection.

00:14:42.630 --> 00:14:48.130
Even though I don't know,
I want to tell him I like him...

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:49.800
Why is that?

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:02.310
I managed to snag
the limited first run edition!

00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:06.230
--Pardon m--
--Oh, it's okay--Sasaki-senpai?

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:07.940
Mya-chan?

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:10.570
What a coincidence.

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:14.700
--Yes. What brings--
--Hey, Shu! Don't run off like that!

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:17.950
Ugh, you always take off immediately.

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:20.420
Because you start talking to the clerk.

00:15:20.420 --> 00:15:22.380
Only for a little bit.

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:24.790
It's never once been a little bit.

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:27.260
Huh?

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:29.510
Hey, wait up!

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:31.930
Oh, thank you, Ogasawara.

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:34.010
Wait, a bag is missing!

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:36.470
--You bought too much.
--Oh, come on.

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:38.810
--I'm beat.
--Mya-chan.

00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:40.690
Are you free right now?

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:42.060
For a little bit.

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:44.020
Let's grab tea, then.

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:50.030
I'll catch up soon,
so wait there with Ogasawara.

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:53.320
Sasaki's sister really runs you ragged.

00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:56.990
Oh, so that was Sasaki-senpai's sister.

00:15:56.990 --> 00:15:58.410
Yeah.

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:01.920
She came to buy clothes
as a present for her boyfriend.

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:05.630
She was using me and Sasaki as mannequins.

00:16:05.630 --> 00:16:08.130
Trying on clothes is tiring.

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:11.130
The cross-dressing competition
prep was rough...

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:12.550
You were in that?!

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:17.350
Yes. Hanzawa-senpai helped me with it.

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:22.560
He ditched his class and helped yours?!

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:25.900
I don't get that dude.

00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:28.190
And somehow his smile is scary.

00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:30.740
The Chairman is a good person.

00:16:30.740 --> 00:16:36.870
He has so many positions and must be
super busy, but he never complains.

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:38.330
True.

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:40.870
You never see him insult anyone.

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:42.040
Huh.

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:44.710
So you respect Hanzawa.

00:16:44.710 --> 00:16:46.710
What about Hirano?

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:49.340
I thought you respected <i>him </i>instead.

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:52.300
Hirano-senpai is...

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:53.760
...kind.

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:55.840
Kind? How so?

00:16:55.840 --> 00:16:58.720
He's strict about studying
and gets angry at people.

00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:01.770
It's kind of him to help you
study in the first place.

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:02.930
Plus...

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:05.020
"delinquent, motherly, blond,
Discipline Committee, handsome, Vice-chairman,
strong fighter, trusted by teachers, etc."

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:07.610
"delinquent, motherly, blond,
Discipline Committee, handsome, Vice-chairman,
strong fighter, trusted by teachers, etc."
...he packs together lots of tropes.

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:10.280
Huh? What was that weird pause about?

00:17:10.280 --> 00:17:15.160
Ah-huh. It's fun to hear other
people's perspectives on them.

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:17.870
Hey, how do you feel about Sasaki?

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:19.160
You hang out a lot, right?

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:22.370
Uh... he's a good <i>senpai</i>.

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:27.460
That's all ya got? Come on now.

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:28.920
Um, well...

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:32.840
You're so close, he'll cancel plans
with me to leave school with you.

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:36.260
Ya gotta have more. Somethin' different
from Hirano and Hanzawa.

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:38.640
Please let it go.

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:43.600
What's that freaky look for?

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:45.850
Don't torment Mya-chan.

00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:47.190
Are you okay, Mya-chan?

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:48.810
Y-Yes.

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:54.150
I didn't. I only asked
if he respects you, dude.

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:55.240
Is that true?

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:56.700
Yes.

00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:58.070
Well?

00:17:58.070 --> 00:18:00.780
How did I wind up here?

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:02.950
I-I think you're a good <i>senpai</i>.

00:18:02.950 --> 00:18:04.370
I see.

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:06.120
That's a big attitude difference.

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:07.420
Shut up.

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:09.380
Hey, what about Ogasawara?

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:10.630
Me?!

00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:13.380
You respect me?

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:18.720
Yes. You're very serious about
your girlfriend. I think it's cool.

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:19.640
Oh.

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:23.350
I'm happy for you.
You have almost no <i>kouhai</i>.

00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:25.270
Shut up!

00:18:25.270 --> 00:18:26.890
Oh, crap!

00:18:27.980 --> 00:18:29.230
I need to go.

00:18:29.230 --> 00:18:31.360
Oh, yeah. Your plans. See ya.

00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:33.400
--Later.
--Plans?

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:37.400
He's cooking dinner with his girlfriend,
so he's going shopping.

00:18:37.400 --> 00:18:39.410
Their families approve, then.

00:18:39.410 --> 00:18:41.870
They're close.

00:18:41.870 --> 00:18:44.200
Mya-chan, do you have plans?

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:46.870
Yes. I'm going to a movie.

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:48.330
Oh, what movie?

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:49.960
Um...

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:51.330
Oh, BL.

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:53.250
Don't guess!

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:54.550
You're right, though.

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:57.340
Can I join you?

00:18:57.340 --> 00:18:58.550
What?!

00:18:59.720 --> 00:19:02.760
Um, are you really sure?

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:05.220
Yup.

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:07.430
It's like we're on a movie date, huh?

00:19:13.570 --> 00:19:16.110
There are a lot of girls here.

00:19:16.110 --> 00:19:20.280
Well, there aren't many pairs of guys.

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:26.080
I thought you'd never choose <i>me</i>.

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:29.330
I mean, you always--

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:31.250
Sorry.

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:33.460
I like you.

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:37.710
I have for so long.

00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:42.180
Apologizing doesn't make it okay, but I...

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:44.640
I don't know what to do!

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:48.310
I like you.

00:19:49.430 --> 00:19:53.270
Senpai, will you accept my feelings?

00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:56.940
That was good.

00:19:56.940 --> 00:19:57.530
--Right, Mya-chan?

00:19:57.530 --> 00:20:00.110
--It was unbelievably good.
--Right, Mya-chan?

00:20:00.110 --> 00:20:04.820
The live action... was better
than I could imagine.

00:20:04.820 --> 00:20:07.080
There can be no better 3D version.

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:12.330
Frankly, I was nervous about the
adaptation, since the original is 2D.

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:16.090
I thought it would
feel off in live action.

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:19.920
I was scared the atmosphere
of the original would be destroyed.

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:25.260
But the reception was good,
so I got curious and came to see it.

00:20:25.260 --> 00:20:28.470
Everything was exactly right.

00:20:28.470 --> 00:20:31.560
Actually, the soul of the
original was in every line,

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:38.110
and the acting and atmosphere did
so much to convey the delicate emotions...

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:40.570
It was really good.

00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:42.820
"I'm glad I worked up
the courage to come."
It was really good.

00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:45.450
It really was.

00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:48.240
I don't think I've borrowed that manga.

00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:51.290
The original is a novel.
Do you want to read it?

00:20:51.290 --> 00:20:54.830
Um, if I can take
a long time to return it.

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:57.250
Oh, because of entrance exams?

00:20:57.250 --> 00:20:58.590
Uh... yeah...

00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:03.550
Actually, I never really
read novels, so I'm uncertain.

00:21:03.550 --> 00:21:05.510
Was anything different from the novel?

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:06.590
Hmm. Well...

00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:09.010
Hey, look. You think they're dating?

00:21:09.010 --> 00:21:11.770
You've been watching too many movies!

00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:14.940
What? I mean, why else
would two guys watch that?

00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:16.600
--You shouldn't make assumptions!
--Mya-chan?

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:18.020
--You shouldn't make assumptions!
--I'm okay.

00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:21.070
They don't mean any harm by it.

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:25.910
Senpai? Um...

00:21:28.990 --> 00:21:32.120
I'm glad we saw this movie.

00:21:36.670 --> 00:21:39.250
Me, too.

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:40.550
I...

00:21:42.090 --> 00:21:46.180
I...

00:21:46.180 --> 00:21:50.890
I feel so at ease around him.

00:21:50.890 --> 00:21:52.390
Huh?

00:21:52.390 --> 00:21:54.270
What's going on?

00:21:56.600 --> 00:22:02.320
I have no guarantee a kiss or
anything else will work out, and yet...

00:22:02.320 --> 00:22:04.610
Senpai...

00:22:04.610 --> 00:22:06.110
Senpai...

00:22:09.820 --> 00:22:13.700
If these feelings aren't
the real deal, what is?

00:23:45.250 --> 00:23:48.170
"Episode 11: 'What Do I Do
About These Feelings?'"
